{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011j5gGREVVvPZMAygzBWcr8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Casting and resolution pipeline for spells and lands.\n2\t\n3\tProvides the full flow from casting a spell or playing a land through\n4\tresolution:\n5\t\n6\t- :func:`cast_spell` — verify timing & legality → move hand to stack →\n7\t  choose targets → pay costs → call ``on_cast`` → push :class:`StackObject`.\n8\t- :func:`play_land` — verify land play remaining → move hand to\n9\t  battlefield → decrement ``land_plays_remaining``.\n10\t- :func:`is_sorcery_speed` / :func:`can_cast_at_instant_speed` — timing\n11\t  helpers used by the casting pipeline.\n12\t\n13\tResolution is embedded in the :class:`StackObject` ``on_resolve`` callback\n14\tcreated by :func:`cast_spell`:\n15\t\n16\t- Call ``card.on_resolve(game)``.\n17\t- Permanents (creature / enchantment / artifact / planeswalker) move from\n18\t  the stack to the battlefield.\n19\t- Non-permanents (instant / sorcery) move to the graveyard.\n20\t\"\"\"\n21\t\n22\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n23\t\n24\tfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\n25\t\n26\tfrom engine.card import CardImpl\n27\tfrom engine.stack import StackObject\n28\tfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, Phase, Zone\n29\tfrom engine.zones import move_zone\n30\t\n31\tif TYPE_CHECKING:\n32\t    from engine.game_state import GameState\n33\t    from engine.player import Player\n34\t\n35\t\n36\t# Card types that represent permanents — these go to the battlefield on resolve.\n37\t_PERMANENT_TYPES: frozenset[CardType] = frozenset({\n38\t    CardType.CREATURE,\n39\t    CardType.ENCHANTMENT,\n40\t    CardType.ARTIFACT,\n41\t    CardType.PLANESWALKER,\n42\t})\n43\t\n44\t\n45\tclass CastingError(Exception):\n46\t    \"\"\"Raised when a spell cast or land play is illegal.\"\"\"\n47\t\n48\t\n49\t# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n50\t# Timing helpers\n51\t# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n52\t\n53\tdef is_sorcery_speed(game: GameState, player: Player) -> bool:\n54\t    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if sorcery-speed timing is met for *player*.\n55\t\n56\t    Sorcery speed requires all of:\n57\t\n58\t    * *player* is the active player.\n59\t    * The current phase is a main phase (``PRECOMBAT_MAIN`` or\n60\t      ``POSTCOMBAT_MAIN``).\n61\t    * The stack is empty.\n62\t    \"\"\"\n63\t    if player is not game.active_player:\n64\t        return False\n65\t    if game.phase not in (Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN):\n66\t        return False\n67\t    if not game.stack.is_empty():\n68\t        return False\n69\t    return True\n70\t\n71\t\n72\tdef can_cast_at_instant_speed(card: CardImpl) -> bool:\n73\t    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *card* may be cast at instant speed.\n74\t\n75\t    A card has instant-speed timing if it is an instant or has the\n76\t    :attr:`~engine.types.Keyword.FLASH` keyword.\n77\t    \"\"\"\n78\t    if CardType.INSTANT in card.card_types:\n79\t        return True\n80\t    if Keyword.FLASH & card.keywords:\n81\t        return True\n82\t    return False\n83\t\n84\t\n85\t# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n86\t# Cost reduction\n87\t# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n88\t\n89\tdef get_cost_reduction(game: GameState, card: CardImpl, controller: Player) -> int:\n90\t    \"\"\"Return the generic mana reduction for casting *card*.\n91\t\n92\t    Queries ``card.cost_reduction(game)`` and clamps the result so that\n93\t    the generic portion of the mana cost cannot go below 0.\n94\t\n95\t    This is a simplified single-card self-reduction model.  Full MTG\n96\t    cost-reduction interactions (Trinisphere, multiple reductions from\n97\t    different sources) are deferred.\n98\t    \"\"\"\n99\t    # Ensure card.controller is set so the hook can reference \"you\" / the\n100\t    # casting player even when the card was never explicitly assigned one.\n101\t    prev_controller = card.controller\n102\t    card.controller = controller\n103\t    raw = card.cost_reduction(game)\n104\t    # Restore previous controller in case the caller doesn't want a\n105\t    # side-effect (get_cost_reduction is a query, not a mutation).\n106\t    card.controller = prev_controller\n107\t    generic = card.mana_cost.generic if card.mana_cost else 0\n108\t    return max(0, min(raw, generic))\n109\t\n110\t\n111\tdef _apply_cost_reduction(cost: ManaCost, reduction: int) -> ManaCost:\n112\t    \"\"\"Return a new :class:`ManaCost` with *reduction* subtracted from generic.\"\"\"\n113\t    new_generic = max(0, cost.generic - reduction)\n114\t    return ManaCost(\n115\t        generic=new_generic,\n116\t        pips=dict(cost.pips),\n117\t        x_count=cost.x_count,\n118\t        hybrid=list(cost.hybrid),\n119\t    )\n120\t\n121\t\n122\t# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n123\t# Cast spell\n124\t# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n125\t\n126\tdef cast_spell(game: GameState, player: Player, card: CardImpl) -> None:\n127\t    \"\"\"Cast *card* from *player*'s hand.\n128\t\n129\t    Pipeline\n130\t    --------\n131\t    1. **Timing check** — instants (and cards with flash) can be cast\n132\t       whenever the player has priority; everything else requires\n133\t       sorcery-speed timing.\n134\t    2. **can_cast** — ask the card whether it can legally be cast.\n135\t    3. **Hand check** — the card must be in the player's hand.\n136\t    4. **Move hand → stack zone** — remove the card from the hand and\n137\t       place it into the player's stack zone.\n138\t    5. **Choose targets** — if the card specifies targets (via\n139\t       :meth:`CardImpl.get_targets`), the player is asked to choose.\n140\t    6. **Mana check / payment** — the player's mana pool must be able to\n141\t       pay the card's mana cost.  If payment fails, the card is rolled\n142\t       back from the stack zone to the hand.\n143\t    7. **Call on_cast** — invoke the card's ``on_cast`` hook.\n144\t    8. **Push StackObject** — push a :class:`StackObject` whose\n145\t       ``on_resolve`` callback handles resolution.\n146\t\n147\t    Raises:\n148\t        CastingError: If any legality check fails.\n149\t    \"\"\"\n150\t    # 1. Timing\n151\t    if not can_cast_at_instant_speed(card) and not is_sorcery_speed(game, player):\n152\t        raise CastingError(\n153\t            f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — sorcery-speed timing not met\"\n154\t        )\n155\t\n156\t    # 2. can_cast\n157\t    if not card.can_cast(game):\n158\t        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — can_cast returned False\")\n159\t\n160\t    # 3. Hand check\n161\t    hand = game.get_hand(player)\n162\t    if not hand.contains(card):\n163\t        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — card not in hand\")\n164\t\n165\t    # 4. Move card from hand to stack zone\n166\t    stack_zone = player.zones[Zone.STACK]\n167\t    hand.remove(card)\n168\t    stack_zone.add(card)\n169\t\n170\t    # Clear any stale colors_spent from a prior cast before new payment.\n171\t    if hasattr(card, \"colors_spent\"):\n172\t        del card.colors_spent\n173\t\n174\t    # 5. Choose targets\n175\t    target_specs = card.get_targets(game)\n176\t    chosen_targets: list[Any] = []\n177\t    if target_specs:\n178\t        for spec in target_specs:\n179\t            target = player.choose_target(target_specs, spec)\n180\t            # Validate against filter_fn if the spec provides one\n181\t            filter_fn = getattr(spec, \"filter_fn\", None)\n182\t            if filter_fn is not None and target is not None:\n183\t                if not filter_fn(target):\n184\t                    stack_zone.remove(card)\n185\t                    hand.add(card)\n186\t                    raise CastingError(\n187\t                        f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — chosen target does not \"\n188\t                        f\"satisfy filter: {getattr(spec, 'description', '')}\"\n189\t                    )\n190\t            chosen_targets.append(target)\n191\t\n192\t    # 5b. Protection check — reject targets that have protection from this\n193\t    #     spell (the T in DEBT).\n194\t    from engine.protection import has_protection_from\n195\t\n196\t    for target in chosen_targets:\n197\t        if has_protection_from(target, card):\n198\t            # Rollback: move card from stack zone back to hand\n199\t            stack_zone.remove(card)\n200\t            hand.add(card)\n201\t            raise CastingError(\n202\t                f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — target has protection from this spell\"\n203\t            )\n204\t\n205\t    # Targets are stored on the StackObject (not the card) and passed\n206\t    # through the resolve pipeline via on_resolve(game, targets=...).\n207\t\n208\t    # 6. Mana check / payment (rollback on failure)\n209\t    # Ensure the card knows its controller so that cost_reduction() hooks\n210\t    # (e.g. Embercleave counting attacking creatures you control) see the\n211\t    # casting player, even for cards that were added to hand without an\n212\t    # explicit controller assignment.\n213\t    if card.controller is None:\n214\t        card.controller = player\n215\t    reduction = get_cost_reduction(game, card, player)\n216\t    effective_cost = _apply_cost_reduction(card.mana_cost, reduction) if reduction > 0 else card.mana_cost\n217\t\n218\t    if not player.mana_pool.can_pay(effective_cost):\n219\t        # Rollback: move card from stack zone back to hand\n220\t        stack_zone.remove(card)\n221\t        hand.add(card)\n222\t        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — insufficient mana\")\n223\t\n224\t    # TODO: Phase 3 — support player choice for generic mana payment to optimize Converge color count\n225\t    player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost)\n226\t\n227\t    # Store colors of mana spent on the card for mechanics like Converge\n228\t    # that care about the colors used to cast the spell.\n229\t    card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n230\t\n231\t    # 7. Call on_cast hook\n232\t    card.on_cast(game)\n233\t\n234\t    # 8. Build on_resolve callback and push StackObject\n235\t    stack_obj = StackObject(\n236\t        source=card,\n237\t        controller=player,\n238\t        targets=chosen_targets,\n239\t        on_resolve=lambda g: None,  # replaced below\n240\t    )\n241\t\n242\t    def _on_resolve(g: GameState) -> None:\n243\t        _resolve_spell(g, card, player, stack_obj)\n244\t\n245\t    stack_obj.on_resolve = _on_resolve\n246\t    game.stack.push(stack_obj)\n247\t\n248\t\n249\t# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n250\t# Cast spell without paying mana cost (free-cast from any zone)\n251\t# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n252\t\n253\t\n254\tdef cast_spell_free(\n255\t    game: GameState,\n256\t    player: Player,\n257\t    card: CardImpl,\n258\t    from_zone: Zone,\n259\t) -> None:\n260\t    \"\"\"Cast *card* without paying its mana cost, using the stack.\n261\t\n262\t    This is used by effects that allow casting from zones other than hand\n263\t    (e.g. exile) without paying mana costs — such as Etali, Primal Storm\n264\t    or cascade.\n265\t\n266\t    Pipeline\n267\t    --------\n268\t    1. **can_cast** — ask the card whether it can legally be cast (same\n269\t       legality as :func:`cast_spell`, minus mana/timing constraints).\n270\t    2. Move *card* from *from_zone* to the stack zone.\n271\t    3. Choose targets (if applicable) with validation and protection check.\n272\t    4. Call ``on_cast`` hook.\n273\t    5. Push a :class:`StackObject` whose ``on_resolve`` callback handles\n274\t       resolution normally (permanents → battlefield, non-permanents →\n275\t       graveyard).\n276\t\n277\t    No timing check or mana payment is performed.  The spell goes on the\n278\t    stack and can be responded to normally (e.g. countered).\n279\t\n280\t    If targeting or other post-move checks fail, the card is rolled back\n281\t    to its source zone.\n282\t\n283\t    Parameters:\n284\t        game: The current game state.\n285\t        player: The player casting the spell.\n286\t        card: The card to cast.\n287\t        from_zone: The zone the card is currently in.\n288\t\n289\t    Raises:\n290\t        CastingError: If the card cannot be found in *from_zone* or\n291\t            legality checks fail.\n292\t    \"\"\"\n293\t    from engine.zones import move_to_zone\n294\t\n295\t    # Ensure controller is set\n296\t    card.controller = player\n297\t    if card.owner is None:\n298\t        card.owner = player\n299\t\n300\t    # 1. can_cast legality (same as cast_spell but skipping mana/timing)\n301\t    if not card.can_cast(game):\n302\t        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — can_cast returned False\")\n303\t\n304\t    # 2. Locate card in source zone\n305\t    source_zone_container = player.zones[from_zone]\n306\t    if not source_zone_container.contains(card):\n307\t        # Try to find the card in any player's zone\n308\t        source_zone_container = None\n309\t        for p in game.players:\n310\t            z = p.zones[from_zone]\n311\t            if z.contains(card):\n312\t                source_zone_container = z\n313\t                break\n314\t\n315\t    if source_zone_container is None or not source_zone_container.contains(card):\n316\t        raise CastingError(\n317\t            f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — card not found in {from_zone.name}\"\n318\t        )\n319\t\n320\t    # Move card from source zone to stack zone\n321\t    stack_zone = player.zones[Zone.STACK]\n322\t    source_zone_container.remove(card)\n323\t    stack_zone.add(card)\n324\t\n325\t    # 3. Choose targets (with rollback on failure)\n326\t    try:\n327\t        target_specs = card.get_targets(game)\n328\t        chosen_targets: list[Any] = []\n329\t        if target_specs:\n330\t            for spec in target_specs:\n331\t                target = player.choose_target(target_specs, spec)\n332\t                # Validate against filter_fn if the spec provides one\n333\t                filter_fn = getattr(spec, \"filter_fn\", None)\n334\t                if filter_fn is not None and target is not None:\n335\t                    if not filter_fn(target):\n336\t                        raise CastingError(\n337\t                            f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — chosen target does not \"\n338\t                            f\"satisfy filter: {getattr(spec, 'description', '')}\"\n339\t                        )\n340\t                chosen_targets.append(target)\n341\t\n342\t        # Protection check — reject targets that have protection from this spell\n343\t        from engine.protection import has_protection_from\n344\t\n345\t        for target in chosen_targets:\n346\t            if has_protection_from(target, card):\n347\t                raise CastingError(\n348\t                    f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — target has protection from this spell\"\n349\t                )\n350\t    except Exception as exc:\n351\t        # Rollback: move card from stack zone back to source zone\n352\t        stack_zone.remove(card)\n353\t        source_zone_container.add(card)\n354\t        raise CastingError(str(exc)) from exc\n355\t\n356\t    # 4. Call on_cast hook\n357\t    card.on_cast(game)\n358\t\n359\t    # 5. Build on_resolve callback and push StackObject\n360\t    stack_obj = StackObject(\n361\t        source=card,\n362\t        controller=player,\n363\t        targets=chosen_targets,\n364\t        on_resolve=lambda g: None,  # replaced below\n365\t    )\n366\t\n367\t    def _on_resolve(g: GameState) -> None:\n368\t        _resolve_spell(g, card, player, stack_obj)\n369\t\n370\t    stack_obj.on_resolve = _on_resolve\n371\t    game.stack.push(stack_obj)\n372\t\n373\t\n374\t# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n375\t# Resolution (called when the stack pops)\n376\t# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n377\t\n378\tdef _resolve_spell(\n379\t    game: GameState,\n380\t    card: CardImpl,\n381\t    player: Player,\n382\t    stack_obj: StackObject,\n383\t) -> None:\n384\t    \"\"\"Resolve *card* cast by *player*.\n385\t\n386\t    1. Call ``card.on_resolve(game, targets=targets)``.\n387\t    2. Remove the card from the stack zone.\n388\t    3. If the card is a permanent type, move it to the battlefield via\n389\t       :func:`~engine.zones.move_to_zone` (which handles trigger/effect\n390\t       registration and the ETB event).\n391\t    4. Otherwise (instant / sorcery), move it to the owner's graveyard.\n392\t    \"\"\"\n393\t    from engine.zones import move_to_zone\n394\t\n395\t    # Read targets from the StackObject — the single source of truth.\n396\t    # Set chosen_targets on the card just before resolution so that\n397\t    # _get_chosen_target helpers (which read via getattr) work.\n398\t    targets = stack_obj.targets\n399\t    if targets is not None:\n400\t        card.chosen_targets = targets  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n401\t\n402\t    card.on_resolve(game)\n403\t\n404\t    if card.card_types & _PERMANENT_TYPES:\n405\t        # Move from stack to battlefield via move_to_zone, which handles\n406\t        # trigger/replacement-effect registration and ENTERS_BATTLEFIELD event.\n407\t        move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)\n408\t    else:\n409\t        # Instant/sorcery: move from stack to graveyard via move_to_zone.\n410\t        move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.GRAVEYARD)\n411\t\n412\t\n413\t# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n414\t# Play land (special action — does not use the stack)\n415\t# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n416\t\n417\tdef play_land(game: GameState, player: Player, land_card: CardImpl) -> None:\n418\t    \"\"\"Play *land_card* from *player*'s hand onto the battlefield.\n419\t\n420\t    Requirements (all must hold):\n421\t\n422\t    * *land_card* has :attr:`CardType.LAND`.\n423\t    * *player* is the active player.\n424\t    * Current phase is a main phase.\n425\t    * The stack is empty.\n426\t    * ``player.land_plays_remaining > 0``.\n427\t    * The card is in the player's hand.\n428\t\n429\t    On success the card moves from hand to battlefield and\n430\t    ``land_plays_remaining`` is decremented.\n431\t\n432\t    Raises:\n433\t        CastingError: If any requirement is not met.\n434\t    \"\"\"\n435\t    # Must be a land\n436\t    if CardType.LAND not in land_card.card_types:\n437\t        raise CastingError(\n438\t            f\"Cannot play {land_card.name!r} as a land — not a land card\"\n439\t        )\n440\t\n441\t    # Sorcery-speed timing (active player, main phase, stack empty)\n442\t    if not is_sorcery_speed(game, player):\n443\t        raise CastingError(\n444\t            f\"Cannot play land {land_card.name!r} — must be active player \"\n445\t            \"during main phase with empty stack\"\n446\t        )\n447\t\n448\t    # Land plays remaining\n449\t    if player.land_plays_remaining <= 0:\n450\t        raise CastingError(\n451\t            f\"Cannot play land {land_card.name!r} — no land plays remaining\"\n452\t        )\n453\t\n454\t    # Card must be in hand\n455\t    hand = game.get_hand(player)\n456\t    if not hand.contains(land_card):\n457\t        raise CastingError(\n458\t            f\"Cannot play land {land_card.name!r} — card not in hand\"\n459\t        )\n460\t\n461\t    # Ensure owner/controller are set so move_to_zone routes correctly.\n462\t    if land_card.owner is None:\n463\t        land_card.owner = player\n464\t    land_card.controller = player\n465\t\n466\t    # Move from hand to battlefield via move_to_zone, which fires\n467\t    # ENTERS_BATTLEFIELD and registers triggers/replacement effects.\n468\t    from engine.zones import move_to_zone\n469\t    move_to_zone(game, land_card, Zone.HAND, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)\n470\t\n471\t    # Decrement land plays\n472\t    player.land_plays_remaining -= 1\n473\t\n474\t\n475\tdef resolve_top(game: GameState) -> None:\n476\t    \"\"\"Resolve the top spell/ability on the stack.\n477\t\n478\t    Pops the top item from the stack, calls its on_resolve callback,\n479\t    then runs state-based actions.  If the stack is empty this is a no-op.\n480\t    \"\"\"\n481\t    if game.stack.is_empty():\n482\t        return\n483\t    from engine.state_based_actions import resolve_state_based_actions\n484\t\n485\t    obj = game.stack.pop()\n486\t    obj.on_resolve(game)\n487\t    resolve_state_based_actions(game)\n488\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21c621d1-2ff1-4c6e-baa9-3ddcfe6a3d2a","uuid":"06925e4d-9300-489b-885f-327441bc68e1","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:58:28.551Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/engine/casting.py","content":"\"\"\"Casting and resolution pipeline for spells and lands.\n\nProvides the full flow from casting a spell or playing a land through\nresolution:\n\n- :func:`cast_spell` — verify timing & legality → move hand to stack →\n  choose targets → pay costs → call ``on_cast`` → push :class:`StackObject`.\n- :func:`play_land` — verify land play remaining → move hand to\n  battlefield → decrement ``land_plays_remaining``.\n- :func:`is_sorcery_speed` / :func:`can_cast_at_instant_speed` — timing\n  helpers used by the casting pipeline.\n\nResolution is embedded in the :class:`StackObject` ``on_resolve`` callback\ncreated by :func:`cast_spell`:\n\n- Call ``card.on_resolve(game)``.\n- Permanents (creature / enchantment / artifact / planeswalker) move from\n  the stack to the battlefield.\n- Non-permanents (instant / sorcery) move to the graveyard.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\n\nfrom engine.card import CardImpl\nfrom engine.stack import StackObject\nfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, Phase, Zone\nfrom engine.zones import move_zone\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from engine.game_state import GameState\n    from engine.player import Player\n\n\n# Card types that represent permanents — these go to the battlefield on resolve.\n_PERMANENT_TYPES: frozenset[CardType] = frozenset({\n    CardType.CREATURE,\n    CardType.ENCHANTMENT,\n    CardType.ARTIFACT,\n    CardType.PLANESWALKER,\n})\n\n\nclass CastingError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Raised when a spell cast or land play is illegal.\"\"\"\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Timing helpers\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef is_sorcery_speed(game: GameState, player: Player) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if sorcery-speed timing is met for *player*.\n\n    Sorcery speed requires all of:\n\n    * *player* is the active player.\n    * The current phase is a main phase (``PRECOMBAT_MAIN`` or\n      ``POSTCOMBAT_MAIN``).\n    * The stack is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if player is not game.active_player:\n        return False\n    if game.phase not in (Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN):\n        return False\n    if not game.stack.is_empty():\n        return False\n    return True\n\n\ndef can_cast_at_instant_speed(card: CardImpl) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *card* may be cast at instant speed.\n\n    A card has instant-speed timing if it is an instant or has the\n    :attr:`~engine.types.Keyword.FLASH` keyword.\n    \"\"\"\n    if CardType.INSTANT in card.card_types:\n        return True\n    if Keyword.FLASH & card.keywords:\n        return True\n    return False\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Cost reduction\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef get_cost_reduction(game: GameState, card: CardImpl, controller: Player) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the generic mana reduction for casting *card*.\n\n    Queries ``card.cost_reduction(game)`` and clamps the result so that\n    the generic portion of the mana cost cannot go below 0.\n\n    This is a simplified single-card self-reduction model.  Full MTG\n    cost-reduction interactions (Trinisphere, multiple reductions from\n    different sources) are deferred.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Ensure card.controller is set so the hook can reference \"you\" / the\n    # casting player even when the card was never explicitly assigned one.\n    prev_controller = card.controller\n    card.controller = controller\n    raw = card.cost_reduction(game)\n    # Restore previous controller in case the caller doesn't want a\n    # side-effect (get_cost_reduction is a query, not a mutation).\n    card.controller = prev_controller\n    generic = card.mana_cost.generic if card.mana_cost else 0\n    return max(0, min(raw, generic))\n\n\ndef _apply_cost_reduction(cost: ManaCost, reduction: int) -> ManaCost:\n    \"\"\"Return a new :class:`ManaCost` with *reduction* subtracted from generic.\"\"\"\n    new_generic = max(0, cost.generic - reduction)\n    return ManaCost(\n        generic=new_generic,\n        pips=dict(cost.pips),\n        x_count=cost.x_count,\n        hybrid=list(cost.hybrid),\n    )\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Cast spell\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef cast_spell(game: GameState, player: Player, card: CardImpl) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Cast *card* from *player*'s hand.\n\n    Pipeline\n    --------\n    1. **Timing check** — instants (and cards with flash) can be cast\n       whenever the player has priority; everything else requires\n       sorcery-speed timing.\n    2. **can_cast** — ask the card whether it can legally be cast.\n    3. **Hand check** — the card must be in the player's hand.\n    4. **Move hand → stack zone** — remove the card from the hand and\n       place it into the player's stack zone.\n    5. **Choose targets** — if the card specifies targets (via\n       :meth:`CardImpl.get_targets`), the player is asked to choose.\n    6. **Mana check / payment** — the player's mana pool must be able to\n       pay the card's mana cost.  If payment fails, the card is rolled\n       back from the stack zone to the hand.\n    7. **Call on_cast** — invoke the card's ``on_cast`` hook.\n    8. **Push StackObject** — push a :class:`StackObject` whose\n       ``on_resolve`` callback handles resolution.\n\n    Raises:\n        CastingError: If any legality check fails.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 1. Timing\n    if not can_cast_at_instant_speed(card) and not is_sorcery_speed(game, player):\n        raise CastingError(\n            f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — sorcery-speed timing not met\"\n        )\n\n    # 2. can_cast\n    if not card.can_cast(game):\n        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — can_cast returned False\")\n\n    # 3. Hand check\n    hand = game.get_hand(player)\n    if not hand.contains(card):\n        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — card not in hand\")\n\n    # 4. Move card from hand to stack zone\n    stack_zone = player.zones[Zone.STACK]\n    hand.remove(card)\n    stack_zone.add(card)\n\n    # Clear any stale colors_spent from a prior cast before new payment.\n    if hasattr(card, \"colors_spent\"):\n        del card.colors_spent\n\n    # 5. Choose targets\n    target_specs = card.get_targets(game)\n    chosen_targets: list[Any] = []\n    if target_specs:\n        for spec in target_specs:\n            target = player.choose_target(target_specs, spec)\n            # Validate against filter_fn if the spec provides one\n            filter_fn = getattr(spec, \"filter_fn\", None)\n            if filter_fn is not None and target is not None:\n                if not filter_fn(target):\n                    stack_zone.remove(card)\n                    hand.add(card)\n                    raise CastingError(\n                        f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — chosen target does not \"\n                        f\"satisfy filter: {getattr(spec, 'description', '')}\"\n                    )\n            chosen_targets.append(target)\n\n    # 5b. Protection check — reject targets that have protection from this\n    #     spell (the T in DEBT).\n    from engine.protection import has_protection_from\n\n    for target in chosen_targets:\n        if has_protection_from(target, card):\n            # Rollback: move card from stack zone back to hand\n            stack_zone.remove(card)\n            hand.add(card)\n            raise CastingError(\n                f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — target has protection from this spell\"\n            )\n\n    # Targets are stored on the StackObject (not the card) and passed\n    # through the resolve pipeline via on_resolve(game, targets=...).\n\n    # 6. Mana check / payment (rollback on failure)\n    # Ensure the card knows its controller so that cost_reduction() hooks\n    # (e.g. Embercleave counting attacking creatures you control) see the\n    # casting player, even for cards that were added to hand without an\n    # explicit controller assignment.\n    if card.controller is None:\n        card.controller = player\n    reduction = get_cost_reduction(game, card, player)\n    effective_cost = _apply_cost_reduction(card.mana_cost, reduction) if reduction > 0 else card.mana_cost\n\n    if not player.mana_pool.can_pay(effective_cost):\n        # Rollback: move card from stack zone back to hand\n        stack_zone.remove(card)\n        hand.add(card)\n        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — insufficient mana\")\n\n    # TODO: Phase 3 — support player choice for generic mana payment to optimize Converge color count\n    player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost)\n\n    # Store colors of mana spent on the card for mechanics like Converge\n    # that care about the colors used to cast the spell.\n    card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n\n    # 7. Call on_cast hook\n    card.on_cast(game)\n\n    # 8. Build on_resolve callback and push StackObject\n    stack_obj = StackObject(\n        source=card,\n        controller=player,\n        targets=chosen_targets,\n        on_resolve=lambda g: None,  # replaced below\n    )\n\n    def _on_resolve(g: GameState) -> None:\n        _resolve_spell(g, card, player, stack_obj)\n\n    stack_obj.on_resolve = _on_resolve\n    game.stack.push(stack_obj)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Cast spell without paying mana cost (free-cast from any zone)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef cast_spell_free(\n    game: GameState,\n    player: Player,\n    card: CardImpl,\n    from_zone: Zone,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Cast *card* without paying its mana cost, using the stack.\n\n    This is used by effects that allow casting from zones other than hand\n    (e.g. exile) without paying mana costs — such as Etali, Primal Storm\n    or cascade.\n\n    Pipeline\n    --------\n    1. **can_cast** — ask the card whether it can legally be cast (same\n       legality as :func:`cast_spell`, minus mana/timing constraints).\n    2. Move *card* from *from_zone* to the stack zone.\n    3. Choose targets (if applicable) with validation and protection check.\n    4. Call ``on_cast`` hook.\n    5. Push a :class:`StackObject` whose ``on_resolve`` callback handles\n       resolution normally (permanents → battlefield, non-permanents →\n       graveyard).\n\n    No timing check or mana payment is performed.  The spell goes on the\n    stack and can be responded to normally (e.g. countered).\n\n    If targeting or other post-move checks fail, the card is rolled back\n    to its source zone.\n\n    Parameters:\n        game: The current game state.\n        player: The player casting the spell.\n        card: The card to cast.\n        from_zone: The zone the card is currently in.\n\n    Raises:\n        CastingError: If the card cannot be found in *from_zone* or\n            legality checks fail.\n    \"\"\"\n    from engine.zones import move_to_zone\n\n    # Ensure controller is set\n    card.controller = player\n    if card.owner is None:\n        card.owner = player\n\n    # 1. can_cast legality (same as cast_spell but skipping mana/timing)\n    if not card.can_cast(game):\n        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — can_cast returned False\")\n\n    # 2. Locate card in source zone\n    source_zone_container = player.zones[from_zone]\n    if not source_zone_container.contains(card):\n        # Try to find the card in any player's zone\n        source_zone_container = None\n        for p in game.players:\n            z = p.zones[from_zone]\n            if z.contains(card):\n                source_zone_container = z\n                break\n\n    if source_zone_container is None or not source_zone_container.contains(card):\n        raise CastingError(\n            f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — card not found in {from_zone.name}\"\n        )\n\n    # Move card from source zone to stack zone\n    stack_zone = player.zones[Zone.STACK]\n    source_zone_container.remove(card)\n    stack_zone.add(card)\n\n    # 3. Choose targets (with rollback on failure)\n    try:\n        target_specs = card.get_targets(game)\n        chosen_targets: list[Any] = []\n        if target_specs:\n            for spec in target_specs:\n                target = player.choose_target(target_specs, spec)\n                # Validate against filter_fn if the spec provides one\n                filter_fn = getattr(spec, \"filter_fn\", None)\n                if filter_fn is not None and target is not None:\n                    if not filter_fn(target):\n                        raise CastingError(\n                            f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — chosen target does not \"\n                            f\"satisfy filter: {getattr(spec, 'description', '')}\"\n                        )\n                chosen_targets.append(target)\n\n        # Protection check — reject targets that have protection from this spell\n        from engine.protection import has_protection_from\n\n        for target in chosen_targets:\n            if has_protection_from(target, card):\n                raise CastingError(\n                    f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — target has protection from this spell\"\n                )\n    except Exception as exc:\n        # Rollback: move card from stack zone back to source zone\n        stack_zone.remove(card)\n        source_zone_container.add(card)\n        raise CastingError(str(exc)) from exc\n\n    # 4. Call on_cast hook\n    card.on_cast(game)\n\n    # 5. Build on_resolve callback and push StackObject\n    stack_obj = StackObject(\n        source=card,\n        controller=player,\n        targets=chosen_targets,\n        on_resolve=lambda g: None,  # replaced below\n    )\n\n    def _on_resolve(g: GameState) -> None:\n        _resolve_spell(g, card, player, stack_obj)\n\n    stack_obj.on_resolve = _on_resolve\n    game.stack.push(stack_obj)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Resolution (called when the stack pops)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef _resolve_spell(\n    game: GameState,\n    card: CardImpl,\n    player: Player,\n    stack_obj: StackObject,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Resolve *card* cast by *player*.\n\n    1. Call ``card.on_resolve(game, targets=targets)``.\n    2. Remove the card from the stack zone.\n    3. If the card is a permanent type, move it to the battlefield via\n       :func:`~engine.zones.move_to_zone` (which handles trigger/effect\n       registration and the ETB event).\n    4. Otherwise (instant / sorcery), move it to the owner's graveyard.\n    \"\"\"\n    from engine.zones import move_to_zone\n\n    # Read targets from the StackObject — the single source of truth.\n    # Set chosen_targets on the card just before resolution so that\n    # _get_chosen_target helpers (which read via getattr) work.\n    targets = stack_obj.targets\n    if targets is not None:\n        card.chosen_targets = targets  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n\n    card.on_resolve(game)\n\n    if card.card_types & _PERMANENT_TYPES:\n        # Move from stack to battlefield via move_to_zone, which handles\n        # trigger/replacement-effect registration and ENTERS_BATTLEFIELD event.\n        move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)\n    else:\n        # Instant/sorcery: move from stack to graveyard via move_to_zone.\n        move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.GRAVEYARD)\n\n\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Play land (special action — does not use the stack)\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef play_land(game: GameState, player: Player, land_card: CardImpl) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Play *land_card* from *player*'s hand onto the battlefield.\n\n    Requirements (all must hold):\n\n    * *land_card* has :attr:`CardType.LAND`.\n    * *player* is the active player.\n    * Current phase is a main phase.\n    * The stack is empty.\n    * ``player.land_plays_remaining > 0``.\n    * The card is in the player's hand.\n\n    On success the card moves from hand to battlefield and\n    ``land_plays_remaining`` is decremented.\n\n    Raises:\n        CastingError: If any requirement is not met.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Must be a land\n    if CardType.LAND not in land_card.card_types:\n        raise CastingError(\n            f\"Cannot play {land_card.name!r} as a land — not a land card\"\n        )\n\n    # Sorcery-speed timing (active player, main phase, stack empty)\n    if not is_sorcery_speed(game, player):\n        raise CastingError(\n            f\"Cannot play land {land_card.name!r} — must be active player \"\n            \"during main phase with empty stack\"\n        )\n\n    # Land plays remaining\n    if player.land_plays_remaining <= 0:\n        raise CastingError(\n            f\"Cannot play land {land_card.name!r} — no land plays remaining\"\n        )\n\n    # Card must be in hand\n    hand = game.get_hand(player)\n    if not hand.contains(land_card):\n        raise CastingError(\n            f\"Cannot play land {land_card.name!r} — card not in hand\"\n        )\n\n    # Ensure owner/controller are set so move_to_zone routes correctly.\n    if land_card.owner is None:\n        land_card.owner = player\n    land_card.controller = player\n\n    # Move from hand to battlefield via move_to_zone, which fires\n    # ENTERS_BATTLEFIELD and registers triggers/replacement effects.\n    from engine.zones import move_to_zone\n    move_to_zone(game, land_card, Zone.HAND, Zone.BATTLEFIELD)\n\n    # Decrement land plays\n    player.land_plays_remaining -= 1\n\n\ndef resolve_top(game: GameState) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Resolve the top spell/ability on the stack.\n\n    Pops the top item from the stack, calls its on_resolve callback,\n    then runs state-based actions.  If the stack is empty this is a no-op.\n    \"\"\"\n    if game.stack.is_empty():\n        return\n    from engine.state_based_actions import resolve_state_based_actions\n\n    obj = game.stack.pop()\n    obj.on_resolve(game)\n    resolve_state_based_actions(game)\n","numLines":488,"startLine":1,"totalLines":488}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_0176ZgTTgLUdavgRkAfoKto8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DWMjpaeaNZMMaqc5VNhErz","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/engine/game.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7607,"cache_read_input_tokens":62500,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7607},"output_tokens":58,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21c621d1-2ff1-4c6e-baa9-3ddcfe6a3d2a","uuid":"4f242cb5-34c1-4eae-b106-f44a29f3d80b","request_id":"req_011CbdNKEUgrezUVZ1FuJdfL"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DWMjpaeaNZMMaqc5VNhErz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Game setup, helper actions, and the full game loop.\n2\t\n3\tProvides the top-level functions for creating, running, and interacting with\n4\ta game of Magic: The Gathering:\n5\t\n6\t- :func:`create_game` — initialise a full game state for two players.\n7\t- Helper actions — module-level functions for common game operations\n8\t  (``deal_damage``, ``destroy``, ``sacrifice``, ``exile``, ``draw_card``,\n9\t  ``discard``, ``create_token``, ``add_counter``, ``remove_counter``,\n10\t  ``tap``, ``untap``).\n11\t- :func:`run_game` — execute turns until the game ends, returning the winner.\n12\t\"\"\"\n13\t\n14\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n15\t\n16\tfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\n17\t\n18\tfrom engine.events import (\n19\t    CreatureDiesReplacementEvent,\n20\t    DealsDamageTriggeredEvent,\n21\t    DrawsCardTriggeredEvent,\n22\t    EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent,\n23\t    GainsLifeTriggeredEvent,\n24\t    LosesLifeTriggeredEvent,\n25\t    PermanentDestroyedReplacementEvent,\n26\t    SacrificeReplacementEvent,\n27\t)\n28\tfrom engine.game_state import GameState\n29\tfrom engine.turn import run_turn\n30\tfrom engine.types import Zone\n31\tfrom engine.zones import move_to_zone\n32\t\n33\tif TYPE_CHECKING:\n34\t    from engine.card import CardImpl, Creature\n35\t    from engine.player import Player\n36\t\n37\t\n38\t# Maximum number of turns before the game is considered a draw.\n39\t# Prevents infinite loops in deterministic or stuck game states.\n40\tMAX_TURNS: int = 1000\n41\t\n42\t\n43\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n44\t# Game creation\n45\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n46\t\n47\tdef create_game(\n48\t    player1: Player,\n49\t    player2: Player,\n50\t    deck1: list[CardImpl],\n51\t    deck2: list[CardImpl],\n52\t) -> GameState:\n53\t    \"\"\"Create and initialise a new two-player game.\n54\t\n55\t    Steps performed:\n56\t\n57\t    1. Set each player's life total to 20.\n58\t    2. Place *deck1* / *deck2* into the respective player's library zone.\n59\t    3. Shuffle each library.\n60\t    4. Draw 7 cards for each player.\n61\t    5. Set the active player to *player1*.\n62\t\n63\t    Card ownership is set so that each card's ``owner`` and ``controller``\n64\t    point to the player whose deck it came from.\n65\t\n66\t    Parameters:\n67\t        player1: The first player (goes first).\n68\t        player2: The second player.\n69\t        deck1: Cards comprising player1's deck.\n70\t        deck2: Cards comprising player2's deck.\n71\t\n72\t    Returns:\n73\t        A fully initialised :class:`GameState` ready for play.\n74\t    \"\"\"\n75\t    # 1. Set life totals\n76\t    player1.life = 20\n77\t    player2.life = 20\n78\t\n79\t    # 2. Place deck cards into libraries and set ownership\n80\t    library1 = player1.zones[Zone.LIBRARY]\n81\t    for card in deck1:\n82\t        card.owner = player1\n83\t        card.controller = player1\n84\t        library1.add(card)\n85\t\n86\t    library2 = player2.zones[Zone.LIBRARY]\n87\t    for card in deck2:\n88\t        card.owner = player2\n89\t        card.controller = player2\n90\t        library2.add(card)\n91\t\n92\t    # 3. Shuffle libraries\n93\t    library1.shuffle()\n94\t    library2.shuffle()\n95\t\n96\t    # Build the game state\n97\t    game = GameState([player1, player2])\n98\t\n99\t    # 4. Draw 7 cards each\n100\t    for _ in range(7):\n101\t        draw_card(game, player1)\n102\t    for _ in range(7):\n103\t        draw_card(game, player2)\n104\t\n105\t    # 5. Active player is player1 (index 0 — already the default)\n106\t    game.active_player_index = 0\n107\t    game.priority_player_index = 0\n108\t\n109\t    return game\n110\t\n111\t\n112\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n113\t# Common helper actions\n114\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n115\t\n116\tdef deal_damage(game: GameState, source: Any, target: Any, amount: int) -> None:\n117\t    \"\"\"Deal *amount* damage from *source* to *target*.\n118\t\n119\t    If *target* has a ``life`` attribute (i.e. is a player), life is reduced.\n120\t    If *target* has a ``damage_marked`` attribute (i.e. is a creature),\n121\t    damage is marked on it.\n122\t\n123\t    Fires :attr:`EventType.DEALS_DAMAGE` via the trigger manager.\n124\t\n125\t    Parameters:\n126\t        game: The current game state.\n127\t        source: The object dealing the damage.\n128\t        target: The player or creature receiving the damage.\n129\t        amount: The amount of damage to deal (must be > 0 to have effect).\n130\t    \"\"\"\n131\t    if amount <= 0:\n132\t        return\n133\t\n134\t    from engine.protection import has_protection_from\n135\t    from engine.types import Keyword\n136\t\n137\t    # Protection prevents damage from sources with the protected-from quality.\n138\t    if has_protection_from(target, source):\n139\t        return\n140\t\n141\t    if hasattr(target, \"life\"):\n142\t        # Target is a player\n143\t        target.life -= amount\n144\t        # Fire damage trigger\n145\t        game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n146\t            game,\n147\t            DealsDamageTriggeredEvent(source=source, target=target, amount=amount),\n148\t        )\n149\t        # Fire loses-life trigger\n150\t        game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n151\t            game,\n152\t            LosesLifeTriggeredEvent(player=target, amount=amount),\n153\t        )\n154\t    elif hasattr(target, \"damage_marked\"):\n155\t        # Target is a creature\n156\t        target.damage_marked += amount\n157\t\n158\t        # Track deathtouch damage for SBA rule 704.5h\n159\t        source_kw = getattr(source, \"keywords\", Keyword(0))\n160\t        if Keyword.DEATHTOUCH in source_kw:\n161\t            target.dealt_deathtouch_damage = True\n162\t\n163\t        # Fire damage trigger\n164\t        game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n165\t            game,\n166\t            DealsDamageTriggeredEvent(source=source, target=target, amount=amount),\n167\t        )\n168\t\n169\t    # Lifelink: controller of source gains life equal to damage dealt\n170\t    source_kw = getattr(source, \"keywords\", Keyword(0))\n171\t    if Keyword.LIFELINK in source_kw:\n172\t        controller = getattr(source, \"controller\", None)\n173\t        if controller is not None and hasattr(controller, \"life\"):\n174\t            controller.life += amount\n175\t\n176\t\n177\tdef destroy(game: GameState, permanent: Any) -> None:\n178\t    \"\"\"Destroy *permanent* — move it from the battlefield to its owner's graveyard.\n179\t\n180\t    Respects replacement effects via :func:`move_to_zone`.\n181\t    Creatures with the ``INDESTRUCTIBLE`` keyword are not destroyed.\n182\t\n183\t    Parameters:\n184\t        game: The current game state.\n185\t        permanent: The permanent to destroy.\n186\t    \"\"\"\n187\t    from engine.types import Keyword\n188\t\n189\t    # Indestructible permanents cannot be destroyed\n190\t    kw = getattr(permanent, \"keywords\", Keyword(0))\n191\t    if Keyword.INDESTRUCTIBLE in kw:\n192\t        return\n193\t\n194\t    controller = getattr(permanent, \"controller\", None)\n195\t    if controller is None:\n196\t        # Fallback: find which player's battlefield contains it\n197\t        for player in game.players:\n198\t            bf = game.get_battlefield(player)\n199\t            if bf.contains(permanent):\n200\t                controller = player\n201\t                break\n202\t    if controller is None:\n203\t        return\n204\t\n205\t    bf = game.get_battlefield(controller)\n206\t    if not bf.contains(permanent):\n207\t        return\n208\t\n209\t    from engine.types import CardType\n210\t\n211\t    card_types = getattr(permanent, \"card_types\", set())\n212\t    is_creature = CardType.CREATURE in card_types\n213\t    owner = getattr(permanent, \"owner\", controller)\n214\t\n215\t    if is_creature:\n216\t        repl_event: CreatureDiesReplacementEvent | PermanentDestroyedReplacementEvent = (\n217\t            CreatureDiesReplacementEvent(\n218\t                creature=permanent, destination=\"graveyard\",\n219\t                controller=controller, owner=owner,\n220\t            )\n221\t        )\n222\t    else:\n223\t        repl_event = PermanentDestroyedReplacementEvent(\n224\t            permanent=permanent, destination=\"graveyard\",\n225\t            controller=controller, owner=owner,\n226\t        )\n227\t\n228\t    move_to_zone(\n229\t        game,\n230\t        permanent,\n231\t        Zone.BATTLEFIELD,\n232\t        Zone.GRAVEYARD,\n233\t        replacement_event=repl_event,\n234\t    )\n235\t\n236\t\n237\tdef sacrifice(game: GameState, player: Player, permanent: Any) -> None:\n238\t    \"\"\"Sacrifice *permanent* — move it from the battlefield to its owner's graveyard.\n239\t\n240\t    Sacrificing cannot be prevented by indestructible or regeneration, but\n241\t    replacement effects that modify zone changes (e.g. \"if this would be\n242\t    put into a graveyard, exile it instead\") still apply via\n243\t    :func:`move_to_zone`.\n244\t\n245\t    Parameters:\n246\t        game: The current game state.\n247\t        player: The player performing the sacrifice.\n248\t        permanent: The permanent to sacrifice.\n249\t    \"\"\"\n250\t    bf = game.get_battlefield(player)\n251\t    if not bf.contains(permanent):\n252\t        return\n253\t\n254\t    owner = getattr(permanent, \"owner\", player)\n255\t    move_to_zone(\n256\t        game,\n257\t        permanent,\n258\t        Zone.BATTLEFIELD,\n259\t        Zone.GRAVEYARD,\n260\t        replacement_event=SacrificeReplacementEvent(\n261\t            permanent=permanent, destination=\"graveyard\",\n262\t            controller=player, owner=owner,\n263\t        ),\n264\t    )\n265\t\n266\t\n267\tdef exile(game: GameState, obj: Any) -> None:\n268\t    \"\"\"Exile *obj* — move it to its owner's exile zone.\n269\t\n270\t    Works for objects on the battlefield, in the graveyard, on the stack,\n271\t    or in hand.\n272\t\n273\t    Parameters:\n274\t        game: The current game state.\n275\t        obj: The game object to exile.\n276\t    \"\"\"\n277\t    # Find which zone the object is currently in\n278\t    source_zone_type = None\n279\t    for player in game.players:\n280\t        for zone_type in Zone:\n281\t            zone = player.zones[zone_type]\n282\t            if zone.contains(obj):\n283\t                source_zone_type = zone_type\n284\t                break\n285\t        if source_zone_type is not None:\n286\t            break\n287\t\n288\t    if source_zone_type is None:\n289\t        return\n290\t\n291\t    move_to_zone(game, obj, source_zone_type, Zone.EXILE)\n292\t\n293\t\n294\tdef draw_card(game: GameState, player: Player) -> Any | None:\n295\t    \"\"\"Draw a card for *player* — move the top card of library to hand.\n296\t\n297\t    If the library is empty, sets ``player.drawn_from_empty_library = True``\n298\t    (SBAs will handle the game loss).\n299\t\n300\t    Fires :attr:`EventType.DRAWS_CARD` via the trigger manager.\n301\t\n302\t    Parameters:\n303\t        game: The current game state.\n304\t        player: The player drawing a card.\n305\t\n306\t    Returns:\n307\t        The drawn card, or ``None`` if the library was empty.\n308\t    \"\"\"\n309\t    library = player.zones[Zone.LIBRARY]\n310\t\n311\t    if len(library) == 0:\n312\t        player.drawn_from_empty_library = True\n313\t        return None\n314\t\n315\t    # Top of library is the last element (index -1)\n316\t    cards = library.top(1)\n317\t    card = cards[0]\n318\t    library.remove(card)\n319\t\n320\t    hand = player.zones[Zone.HAND]\n321\t    hand.add(card)\n322\t\n323\t    # Track cards drawn this turn\n324\t    if not hasattr(player, \"cards_drawn_this_turn\"):\n325\t        player.cards_drawn_this_turn = 0\n326\t    player.cards_drawn_this_turn += 1\n327\t\n328\t    # Fire trigger (only if game has a trigger_manager — may not during setup)\n329\t    if hasattr(game, \"trigger_manager\"):\n330\t        game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n331\t            game,\n332\t            DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player=player, card=card),\n333\t        )\n334\t\n335\t    return card\n336\t\n337\t\n338\tdef discard(game: GameState, player: Player, card: Any) -> None:\n339\t    \"\"\"Discard *card* from *player*'s hand to the owner's graveyard.\n340\t\n341\t    Parameters:\n342\t        game: The current game state.\n343\t        player: The player discarding.\n344\t        card: The card to discard (must be in the player's hand).\n345\t    \"\"\"\n346\t    hand = game.get_hand(player)\n347\t    if not hand.contains(card):\n348\t        return\n349\t\n350\t    move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.HAND, Zone.GRAVEYARD)\n351\t\n352\t\n353\tdef create_token(game: GameState, player: Player, token: Any) -> None:\n354\t    \"\"\"Create a token on the battlefield under *player*'s control.\n355\t\n356\t    Sets ``is_token = True`` on the token, along with ``owner`` and\n357\t    ``controller``.  Uses :func:`move_to_zone` for entering-battlefield\n358\t    hooks (trigger/replacement-effect registration and ETB event).\n359\t\n360\t    Parameters:\n361\t        game: The current game state.\n362\t        player: The player who controls the token.\n363\t        token: The token object to place on the battlefield.\n364\t    \"\"\"\n365\t    token.is_token = True\n366\t    token.owner = player\n367\t    token.controller = player\n368\t\n369\t    # Tokens don't come from an existing zone — add directly and fire hooks.\n370\t    # Ordering matches move_to_zone: fire ETB *before* registering the token's\n371\t    # own triggers so a token's ETB trigger doesn't self-fire on entry.\n372\t    battlefield = game.get_battlefield(player)\n373\t    battlefield.add(token)\n374\t\n375\t    game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n376\t        game,\n377\t        EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(permanent=token, controller=player),\n378\t    )\n379\t\n380\t    # Register triggers/replacement effects after the ETB event.\n381\t    if hasattr(token, \"register_triggers\"):\n382\t        token.register_triggers(game)\n383\t    if hasattr(token, \"register_replacement_effects\"):\n384\t        token.register_replacement_effects(game)\n385\t\n386\t\n387\tdef add_counter(\n388\t    game: GameState,\n389\t    permanent: Any,\n390\t    counter_type: str,\n391\t    amount: int = 1,\n392\t) -> None:\n393\t    \"\"\"Add *amount* counters of *counter_type* to *permanent*.\n394\t\n395\t    Supports ``\"+1/+1\"`` and ``\"-1/-1\"`` counter types via the\n396\t    ``plus_one_counters`` / ``minus_one_counters`` attributes.  For other\n397\t    counter types, uses a generic ``counters`` dict.\n398\t\n399\t    Parameters:\n400\t        game: The current game state.\n401\t        permanent: The permanent to add counters to.\n402\t        counter_type: The type of counter (e.g. ``\"+1/+1\"``, ``\"-1/-1\"``,\n403\t            ``\"loyalty\"``, ``\"charge\"``).\n404\t        amount: Number of counters to add (default 1).\n405\t    \"\"\"\n406\t    if amount <= 0:\n407\t        return\n408\t\n409\t    if counter_type == \"+1/+1\" and hasattr(permanent, \"plus_one_counters\"):\n410\t        permanent.plus_one_counters += amount\n411\t    elif counter_type == \"-1/-1\" and hasattr(permanent, \"minus_one_counters\"):\n412\t        permanent.minus_one_counters += amount\n413\t    elif counter_type == \"loyalty\" and hasattr(permanent, \"loyalty\"):\n414\t        permanent.loyalty += amount\n415\t    else:\n416\t        # Generic counter storage\n417\t        if not hasattr(permanent, \"counters\"):\n418\t            permanent.counters = {}\n419\t        permanent.counters[counter_type] = permanent.counters.get(counter_type, 0) + amount\n420\t\n421\t\n422\tdef remove_counter(\n423\t    game: GameState,\n424\t    permanent: Any,\n425\t    counter_type: str,\n426\t    amount: int = 1,\n427\t) -> None:\n428\t    \"\"\"Remove *amount* counters of *counter_type* from *permanent*.\n429\t\n430\t    Will not reduce below zero.\n431\t\n432\t    Parameters:\n433\t        game: The current game state.\n434\t        permanent: The permanent to remove counters from.\n435\t        counter_type: The type of counter to remove.\n436\t        amount: Number of counters to remove (default 1).\n437\t    \"\"\"\n438\t    if amount <= 0:\n439\t        return\n440\t\n441\t    if counter_type == \"+1/+1\" and hasattr(permanent, \"plus_one_counters\"):\n442\t        permanent.plus_one_counters = max(0, permanent.plus_one_counters - amount)\n443\t    elif counter_type == \"-1/-1\" and hasattr(permanent, \"minus_one_counters\"):\n444\t        permanent.minus_one_counters = max(0, permanent.minus_one_counters - amount)\n445\t    elif counter_type == \"loyalty\" and hasattr(permanent, \"loyalty\"):\n446\t        permanent.loyalty = max(0, permanent.loyalty - amount)\n447\t    else:\n448\t        if hasattr(permanent, \"counters\") and counter_type in permanent.counters:\n449\t            permanent.counters[counter_type] = max(\n450\t                0, permanent.counters[counter_type] - amount\n451\t            )\n452\t\n453\t\n454\tdef tap(game: GameState, permanent: Any) -> None:\n455\t    \"\"\"Tap *permanent* — set ``is_tapped = True``.\n456\t\n457\t    Parameters:\n458\t        game: The current game state.\n459\t        permanent: The permanent to tap.\n460\t    \"\"\"\n461\t    if hasattr(permanent, \"is_tapped\"):\n462\t        permanent.is_tapped = True\n463\t\n464\t\n465\tdef untap(game: GameState, permanent: Any) -> None:\n466\t    \"\"\"Untap *permanent* — set ``is_tapped = False``.\n467\t\n468\t    Parameters:\n469\t        game: The current game state.\n470\t        permanent: The permanent to untap.\n471\t    \"\"\"\n472\t    if hasattr(permanent, \"is_tapped\"):\n473\t        permanent.is_tapped = False\n474\t\n475\t\n476\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n477\t# Game loop\n478\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n479\t\n480\tdef run_game(game: GameState) -> Player | None:\n481\t    \"\"\"Run the game loop until the game ends.\n482\t\n483\t    Executes :func:`~engine.turn.run_turn` in a loop, checking\n484\t    :attr:`GameState.is_game_over` after each turn.  State-based actions\n485\t    are resolved before and after each turn to catch game-ending conditions\n486\t    even when the priority loop auto-passes.\n487\t\n488\t    Includes a safety limit of :data:`MAX_TURNS` to prevent infinite loops\n489\t    in deterministic or stuck game states.\n490\t\n491\t    Parameters:\n492\t        game: The game state to run.\n493\t\n494\t    Returns:\n495\t        The winning player, or ``None`` if the game ended in a draw (or\n496\t        hit the turn limit).\n497\t    \"\"\"\n498\t    from engine.state_based_actions import resolve_state_based_actions\n499\t\n500\t    while not game.is_game_over and game.turn_number <= MAX_TURNS:\n501\t        # Check SBAs before the turn (catches pre-existing conditions)\n502\t        resolve_state_based_actions(game)\n503\t        _check_game_over(game)\n504\t        if game.is_game_over:\n505\t            break\n506\t\n507\t        run_turn(game)\n508\t\n509\t        # Check SBAs after the turn\n510\t        resolve_state_based_actions(game)\n511\t        _check_game_over(game)\n512\t\n513\t    return game.winner\n514\t\n515\t\n516\tdef _check_game_over(game: GameState) -> None:\n517\t    \"\"\"Check whether the game has ended and update ``game.is_game_over`` / ``game.winner``.\n518\t\n519\t    The game ends when:\n520\t    - One player has lost (``has_lost``): the other player wins.\n521\t    - Both players have lost: the game is a draw (``winner = None``).\n522\t    - The turn limit is exceeded: the game is a draw.\n523\t    \"\"\"\n524\t    lost_players = [p for p in game.players if p.has_lost]\n525\t\n526\t    if len(lost_players) == len(game.players):\n527\t        # All players have lost — draw\n528\t        game.is_game_over = True\n529\t        game.winner = None\n530\t    elif len(lost_players) == 1:\n531\t        # One player lost — the other wins\n532\t        game.is_game_over = True\n533\t        game.winner = [p for p in game.players if not p.has_lost][0]\n534\t    elif game.turn_number > MAX_TURNS:\n535\t        # Turn limit exceeded — draw\n536\t        game.is_game_over = True\n537\t        game.winner = None\n538\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21c621d1-2ff1-4c6e-baa9-3ddcfe6a3d2a","uuid":"486a5b6e-a39b-46c8-9555-1ef2e1aa1234","timestamp":"2026-06-01T22:58:30.466Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/engine/game.py","content":"\"\"\"Game setup, helper actions, and the full game loop.\n\nProvides the top-level functions for creating, running, and interacting with\na game of Magic: The Gathering:\n\n- :func:`create_game` — initialise a full game state for two players.\n- Helper actions — module-level functions for common game operations\n  (``deal_damage``, ``destroy``, ``sacrifice``, ``exile``, ``draw_card``,\n  ``discard``, ``create_token``, ``add_counter``, ``remove_counter``,\n  ``tap``, ``untap``).\n- :func:`run_game` — execute turns until the game ends, returning the winner.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any\n\nfrom engine.events import (\n    CreatureDiesReplacementEvent,\n    DealsDamageTriggeredEvent,\n    DrawsCardTriggeredEvent,\n    EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent,\n    GainsLifeTriggeredEvent,\n    LosesLifeTriggeredEvent,\n    PermanentDestroyedReplacementEvent,\n    SacrificeReplacementEvent,\n)\nfrom engine.game_state import GameState\nfrom engine.turn import run_turn\nfrom engine.types import Zone\nfrom engine.zones import move_to_zone\n\nif TYPE_CHECKING:\n    from engine.card import CardImpl, Creature\n    from engine.player import Player\n\n\n# Maximum number of turns before the game is considered a draw.\n# Prevents infinite loops in deterministic or stuck game states.\nMAX_TURNS: int = 1000\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Game creation\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef create_game(\n    player1: Player,\n    player2: Player,\n    deck1: list[CardImpl],\n    deck2: list[CardImpl],\n) -> GameState:\n    \"\"\"Create and initialise a new two-player game.\n\n    Steps performed:\n\n    1. Set each player's life total to 20.\n    2. Place *deck1* / *deck2* into the respective player's library zone.\n    3. Shuffle each library.\n    4. Draw 7 cards for each player.\n    5. Set the active player to *player1*.\n\n    Card ownership is set so that each card's ``owner`` and ``controller``\n    point to the player whose deck it came from.\n\n    Parameters:\n        player1: The first player (goes first).\n        player2: The second player.\n        deck1: Cards comprising player1's deck.\n        deck2: Cards comprising player2's deck.\n\n    Returns:\n        A fully initialised :class:`GameState` ready for play.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 1. Set life totals\n    player1.life = 20\n    player2.life = 20\n\n    # 2. Place deck cards into libraries and set ownership\n    library1 = player1.zones[Zone.LIBRARY]\n    for card in deck1:\n        card.owner = player1\n        card.controller = player1\n        library1.add(card)\n\n    library2 = player2.zones[Zone.LIBRARY]\n    for card in deck2:\n        card.owner = player2\n        card.controller = player2\n        library2.add(card)\n\n    # 3. Shuffle libraries\n    library1.shuffle()\n    library2.shuffle()\n\n    # Build the game state\n    game = GameState([player1, player2])\n\n    # 4. Draw 7 cards each\n    for _ in range(7):\n        draw_card(game, player1)\n    for _ in range(7):\n        draw_card(game, player2)\n\n    # 5. Active player is player1 (index 0 — already the default)\n    game.active_player_index = 0\n    game.priority_player_index = 0\n\n    return game\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Common helper actions\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef deal_damage(game: GameState, source: Any, target: Any, amount: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Deal *amount* damage from *source* to *target*.\n\n    If *target* has a ``life`` attribute (i.e. is a player), life is reduced.\n    If *target* has a ``damage_marked`` attribute (i.e. is a creature),\n    damage is marked on it.\n\n    Fires :attr:`EventType.DEALS_DAMAGE` via the trigger manager.\n\n    Parameters:\n        game: The current game state.\n        source: The object dealing the damage.\n        target: The player or creature receiving the damage.\n        amount: The amount of damage to deal (must be > 0 to have effect).\n    \"\"\"\n    if amount <= 0:\n        return\n\n    from engine.protection import has_protection_from\n    from engine.types import Keyword\n\n    # Protection prevents damage from sources with the protected-from quality.\n    if has_protection_from(target, source):\n        return\n\n    if hasattr(target, \"life\"):\n        # Target is a player\n        target.life -= amount\n        # Fire damage trigger\n        game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n            game,\n            DealsDamageTriggeredEvent(source=source, target=target, amount=amount),\n        )\n        # Fire loses-life trigger\n        game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n            game,\n            LosesLifeTriggeredEvent(player=target, amount=amount),\n        )\n    elif hasattr(target, \"damage_marked\"):\n        # Target is a creature\n        target.damage_marked += amount\n\n        # Track deathtouch damage for SBA rule 704.5h\n        source_kw = getattr(source, \"keywords\", Keyword(0))\n        if Keyword.DEATHTOUCH in source_kw:\n            target.dealt_deathtouch_damage = True\n\n        # Fire damage trigger\n        game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n            game,\n            DealsDamageTriggeredEvent(source=source, target=target, amount=amount),\n        )\n\n    # Lifelink: controller of source gains life equal to damage dealt\n    source_kw = getattr(source, \"keywords\", Keyword(0))\n    if Keyword.LIFELINK in source_kw:\n        controller = getattr(source, \"controller\", None)\n        if controller is not None and hasattr(controller, \"life\"):\n            controller.life += amount\n\n\ndef destroy(game: GameState, permanent: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Destroy *permanent* — move it from the battlefield to its owner's graveyard.\n\n    Respects replacement effects via :func:`move_to_zone`.\n    Creatures with the ``INDESTRUCTIBLE`` keyword are not destroyed.\n\n    Parameters:\n        game: The current game state.\n        permanent: The permanent to destroy.\n    \"\"\"\n    from engine.types import Keyword\n\n    # Indestructible permanents cannot be destroyed\n    kw = getattr(permanent, \"keywords\", Keyword(0))\n    if Keyword.INDESTRUCTIBLE in kw:\n        return\n\n    controller = getattr(permanent, \"controller\", None)\n    if controller is None:\n        # Fallback: find which player's battlefield contains it\n        for player in game.players:\n            bf = game.get_battlefield(player)\n            if bf.contains(permanent):\n                controller = player\n                break\n    if controller is None:\n        return\n\n    bf = game.get_battlefield(controller)\n    if not bf.contains(permanent):\n        return\n\n    from engine.types import CardType\n\n    card_types = getattr(permanent, \"card_types\", set())\n    is_creature = CardType.CREATURE in card_types\n    owner = getattr(permanent, \"owner\", controller)\n\n    if is_creature:\n        repl_event: CreatureDiesReplacementEvent | PermanentDestroyedReplacementEvent = (\n            CreatureDiesReplacementEvent(\n                creature=permanent, destination=\"graveyard\",\n                controller=controller, owner=owner,\n            )\n        )\n    else:\n        repl_event = PermanentDestroyedReplacementEvent(\n            permanent=permanent, destination=\"graveyard\",\n            controller=controller, owner=owner,\n        )\n\n    move_to_zone(\n        game,\n        permanent,\n        Zone.BATTLEFIELD,\n        Zone.GRAVEYARD,\n        replacement_event=repl_event,\n    )\n\n\ndef sacrifice(game: GameState, player: Player, permanent: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Sacrifice *permanent* — move it from the battlefield to its owner's graveyard.\n\n    Sacrificing cannot be prevented by indestructible or regeneration, but\n    replacement effects that modify zone changes (e.g. \"if this would be\n    put into a graveyard, exile it instead\") still apply via\n    :func:`move_to_zone`.\n\n    Parameters:\n        game: The current game state.\n        player: The player performing the sacrifice.\n        permanent: The permanent to sacrifice.\n    \"\"\"\n    bf = game.get_battlefield(player)\n    if not bf.contains(permanent):\n        return\n\n    owner = getattr(permanent, \"owner\", player)\n    move_to_zone(\n        game,\n        permanent,\n        Zone.BATTLEFIELD,\n        Zone.GRAVEYARD,\n        replacement_event=SacrificeReplacementEvent(\n            permanent=permanent, destination=\"graveyard\",\n            controller=player, owner=owner,\n        ),\n    )\n\n\ndef exile(game: GameState, obj: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Exile *obj* — move it to its owner's exile zone.\n\n    Works for objects on the battlefield, in the graveyard, on the stack,\n    or in hand.\n\n    Parameters:\n        game: The current game state.\n        obj: The game object to exile.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Find which zone the object is currently in\n    source_zone_type = None\n    for player in game.players:\n        for zone_type in Zone:\n            zone = player.zones[zone_type]\n            if zone.contains(obj):\n                source_zone_type = zone_type\n                break\n        if source_zone_type is not None:\n            break\n\n    if source_zone_type is None:\n        return\n\n    move_to_zone(game, obj, source_zone_type, Zone.EXILE)\n\n\ndef draw_card(game: GameState, player: Player) -> Any | None:\n    \"\"\"Draw a card for *player* — move the top card of library to hand.\n\n    If the library is empty, sets ``player.drawn_from_empty_library = True``\n    (SBAs will handle the game loss).\n\n    Fires :attr:`EventType.DRAWS_CARD` via the trigger manager.\n\n    Parameters:\n        game: The current game state.\n        player: The player drawing a card.\n\n    Returns:\n        The drawn card, or ``None`` if the library was empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    library = player.zones[Zone.LIBRARY]\n\n    if len(library) == 0:\n        player.drawn_from_empty_library = True\n        return None\n\n    # Top of library is the last element (index -1)\n    cards = library.top(1)\n    card = cards[0]\n    library.remove(card)\n\n    hand = player.zones[Zone.HAND]\n    hand.add(card)\n\n    # Track cards drawn this turn\n    if not hasattr(player, \"cards_drawn_this_turn\"):\n        player.cards_drawn_this_turn = 0\n    player.cards_drawn_this_turn += 1\n\n    # Fire trigger (only if game has a trigger_manager — may not during setup)\n    if hasattr(game, \"trigger_manager\"):\n        game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n            game,\n            DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player=player, card=card),\n        )\n\n    return card\n\n\ndef discard(game: GameState, player: Player, card: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Discard *card* from *player*'s hand to the owner's graveyard.\n\n    Parameters:\n        game: The current game state.\n        player: The player discarding.\n        card: The card to discard (must be in the player's hand).\n    \"\"\"\n    hand = game.get_hand(player)\n    if not hand.contains(card):\n        return\n\n    move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.HAND, Zone.GRAVEYARD)\n\n\ndef create_token(game: GameState, player: Player, token: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Create a token on the battlefield under *player*'s control.\n\n    Sets ``is_token = True`` on the token, along with ``owner`` and\n    ``controller``.  Uses :func:`move_to_zone` for entering-battlefield\n    hooks (trigger/replacement-effect registration and ETB event).\n\n    Parameters:\n        game: The current game state.\n        player: The player who controls the token.\n        token: The token object to place on the battlefield.\n    \"\"\"\n    token.is_token = True\n    token.owner = player\n    token.controller = player\n\n    # Tokens don't come from an existing zone — add directly and fire hooks.\n    # Ordering matches move_to_zone: fire ETB *before* registering the token's\n    # own triggers so a token's ETB trigger doesn't self-fire on entry.\n    battlefield = game.get_battlefield(player)\n    battlefield.add(token)\n\n    game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n        game,\n        EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(permanent=token, controller=player),\n    )\n\n    # Register triggers/replacement effects after the ETB event.\n    if hasattr(token, \"register_triggers\"):\n        token.register_triggers(game)\n    if hasattr(token, \"register_replacement_effects\"):\n        token.register_replacement_effects(game)\n\n\ndef add_counter(\n    game: GameState,\n    permanent: Any,\n    counter_type: str,\n    amount: int = 1,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Add *amount* counters of *counter_type* to *permanent*.\n\n    Supports ``\"+1/+1\"`` and ``\"-1/-1\"`` counter types via the\n    ``plus_one_counters`` / ``minus_one_counters`` attributes.  For other\n    counter types, uses a generic ``counters`` dict.\n\n    Parameters:\n        game: The current game state.\n        permanent: The permanent to add counters to.\n        counter_type: The type of counter (e.g. ``\"+1/+1\"``, ``\"-1/-1\"``,\n            ``\"loyalty\"``, ``\"charge\"``).\n        amount: Number of counters to add (default 1).\n    \"\"\"\n    if amount <= 0:\n        return\n\n    if counter_type == \"+1/+1\" and hasattr(permanent, \"plus_one_counters\"):\n        permanent.plus_one_counters += amount\n    elif counter_type == \"-1/-1\" and hasattr(permanent, \"minus_one_counters\"):\n        permanent.minus_one_counters += amount\n    elif counter_type == \"loyalty\" and hasattr(permanent, \"loyalty\"):\n        permanent.loyalty += amount\n    else:\n        # Generic counter storage\n        if not hasattr(permanent, \"counters\"):\n            permanent.counters = {}\n        permanent.counters[counter_type] = permanent.counters.get(counter_type, 0) + amount\n\n\ndef remove_counter(\n    game: GameState,\n    permanent: Any,\n    counter_type: str,\n    amount: int = 1,\n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Remove *amount* counters of *counter_type* from *permanent*.\n\n    Will not reduce below zero.\n\n    Parameters:\n        game: The current game state.\n        permanent: The permanent to remove counters from.\n        counter_type: The type of counter to remove.\n        amount: Number of counters to remove (default 1).\n    \"\"\"\n    if amount <= 0:\n        return\n\n    if counter_type == \"+1/+1\" and hasattr(permanent, \"plus_one_counters\"):\n        permanent.plus_one_counters = max(0, permanent.plus_one_counters - amount)\n    elif counter_type == \"-1/-1\" and hasattr(permanent, \"minus_one_counters\"):\n        permanent.minus_one_counters = max(0, permanent.minus_one_counters - amount)\n    elif counter_type == \"loyalty\" and hasattr(permanent, \"loyalty\"):\n        permanent.loyalty = max(0, permanent.loyalty - amount)\n    else:\n        if hasattr(permanent, \"counters\") and counter_type in permanent.counters:\n            permanent.counters[counter_type] = max(\n                0, permanent.counters[counter_type] - amount\n            )\n\n\ndef tap(game: GameState, permanent: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Tap *permanent* — set ``is_tapped = True``.\n\n    Parameters:\n        game: The current game state.\n        permanent: The permanent to tap.\n    \"\"\"\n    if hasattr(permanent, \"is_tapped\"):\n        permanent.is_tapped = True\n\n\ndef untap(game: GameState, permanent: Any) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Untap *permanent* — set ``is_tapped = False``.\n\n    Parameters:\n        game: The current game state.\n        permanent: The permanent to untap.\n    \"\"\"\n    if hasattr(permanent, \"is_tapped\"):\n        permanent.is_tapped = False\n\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Game loop\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef run_game(game: GameState) -> Player | None:\n    \"\"\"Run the game loop until the game ends.\n\n    Executes :func:`~engine.turn.run_turn` in a loop, checking\n    :attr:`GameState.is_game_over` after each turn.  State-based actions\n    are resolved before and after each turn to catch game-ending conditions\n    even when the priority loop auto-passes.\n\n    Includes a safety limit of :data:`MAX_TURNS` to prevent infinite loops\n    in deterministic or stuck game states.\n\n    Parameters:\n        game: The game state to run.\n\n    Returns:\n        The winning player, or ``None`` if the game ended in a draw (or\n        hit the turn limit).\n    \"\"\"\n    from engine.state_based_actions import resolve_state_based_actions\n\n    while not game.is_game_over and game.turn_number <= MAX_TURNS:\n        # Check SBAs before the turn (catches pre-existing conditions)\n        resolve_state_based_actions(game)\n        _check_game_over(game)\n        if game.is_game_over:\n            break\n\n        run_turn(game)\n\n        # Check SBAs after the turn\n        resolve_state_based_actions(game)\n        _check_game_over(game)\n\n    return game.winner\n\n\ndef _check_game_over(game: GameState) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Check whether the game has ended and update ``game.is_game_over`` / ``game.winner``.\n\n    The game ends when:\n    - One player has lost (``has_lost``): the other player wins.\n    - Both players have lost: the game is a draw (``winner = None``).\n    - The turn limit is exceeded: the game is a draw.\n    \"\"\"\n    lost_players = [p for p in game.players if p.has_lost]\n\n    if len(lost_players) == len(game.players):\n        # All players have lost — draw\n        game.is_game_over = True\n        game.winner = None\n    elif len(lost_players) == 1:\n        # One player lost — the other wins\n        game.is_game_over = True\n        game.winner = [p for p in game.players if not p.has_lost][0]\n    elif game.turn_number > MAX_TURNS:\n        # Turn limit exceeded — draw\n        game.is_game_over = True\n        game.winner = None\n","numLines":538,"startLine":1,"totalLines":538}}}
