{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's explicit task: \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly. You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\"\n\n   CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS (must be preserved verbatim):\n   - \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score.\"\n   - From AGENTS.md: \"Card location invariant — Each card's canonical implementation class must remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`. Do not move or rename card directories.\"\n   - \"Staged-test integrity — Treat `engine_tests/` as read-only... do not modify or delete any existing FDN reference test file at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py` (you may read them as examples, but never edit them)... Your own SOS tests belong at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\"\n   - \"Additive-only engine modifications — You may add new methods, classes, helpers, and files inside `engine/`. You may modify the bodies of existing functions to implement card behavior. You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/`.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG card implementation framework with `CardImpl` base class and subclasses (Creature, Instant, Sorcery, Planeswalker, Land, Enchantment, Artifact, etc.)\n   - Hook methods: `can_cast`, `cost_reduction(game)->int`, `on_cast`, `on_resolve`, `get_targets`, `register_triggers`, `register_replacement_effects`, `get_activated_abilities`, `get_modes`, `get_loyalty_abilities` (Planeswalker), `get_mana_abilities` (Land)\n   - Triggered abilities: `TriggerManager.register/fire_event`, `TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller)`, APNAP ordering\n   - Replacement effects: `ReplacementManager`, `ReplacementEffect`, \"instead\" semantics, `move_to_zone` redirection via `destination`/`prevented`\n   - Continuous effects: 7-layer system, `ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration)`, `DURATION_END_OF_TURN`/`DURATION_PERMANENT`, `EffectManager.add/apply_all`\n   - Converge mechanic (`colors_spent`), cost reduction (`cost_reduction` hook, only reduces generic, clamped to >=0)\n   - Mechanics needing engine extensions: Converge, Surveil, Miracle, Casualty, Affinity, Paradigm, Prepared, coin flips, skip turns\n   - Keyword flags (enum.Flag): FLYING, REACH, HASTE, VIGILANCE, DEATHTOUCH, etc. (only 16 evergreen keywords defined; Surveil/Affinity/etc. are listed in specs but NOT in Keyword enum)\n   - DeterministicPlayer with FIFO scripts for `choose`, `choose_target`, `choose_yes_no`, `choose_card`, `assign_damage_order`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_{1,4,13,57,97,120,201,226,245,257}/card_spec.json` and `card_impl.py` — the targets. All impl files are empty stubs with `pass`. Card classes needed:\n     - sos_1: `TheDawningArchaic` (Legendary Creature Avatar, {10}, 7/7, Reach; cost {1} less per instant/sorcery in GY; attack trigger to free-cast inst/sorc from GY, exile-instead replacement)\n     - sos_4: `TogetherAsOne` (Sorcery {6}, Converge: target player draws X, deals X damage to any target, gain X life)\n     - sos_13: `EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares` (Creature Cat Cleric // Instant split; ETB token + Prepared mechanic)\n     - sos_57: `ManaSculpt` (Instant {1}{U}{U}, counter target spell; if control Wizard, add C equal to mana spent at next main phase)\n     - sos_97: `RalZarekGuestLecturer` (Planeswalker {1}{B}{B}, 3 loyalty; +1 Surveil 2, -1 discard, -2 reanimate MV<=3, -7 coin flips/skip turns)\n     - sos_120: `ImprovisationCapstone` (Sorcery Lesson {5}{R}{R}, exile until MV 4+, cast free; Paradigm)\n     - sos_201: `LoreholdTheHistorian` (Legendary Creature Elder Dragon {3}{R}{W}, 5/5, Flying haste; grants miracle {2} to inst/sorc in hand; opponent upkeep loot)\n     - sos_226: `SilverquillTheDisputant` (Legendary Creature Elder Dragon {2}{W}{B}, 4/4, Flying vigilance; grants casualty 1 to inst/sorc you cast)\n     - sos_245: `WitherbloomTheBalancer` (Legendary Creature Elder Dragon {6}{B}{G}, 5/5, Flying deathtouch; Affinity for creatures; grants affinity for creatures to inst/sorc)\n     - sos_257: `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex` (Land; {T}:Add C; {T},pay 1 life: add any color for inst/sorc; {5}: becomes 2/4 Wizard creature with pump on inst/sorc cast)\n   - `/workspace/engine/card.py` — `CardImpl` hooks, `Creature` (base_power/toughness, modified_power, plus_one_counters, `_reset_characteristics`, `power`/`toughness` properties), `Planeswalker` (starting_loyalty, loyalty, get_loyalty_abilities), `Land` (get_mana_abilities), dataclasses ActivatedAbility/LoyaltyAbility/ManaAbility/ContinuousEffect/Mode.\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — `cast_spell` (sets `card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)` after payment; calls `on_cast`; pushes StackObject with `_resolve_spell`). `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` for free casts. `get_cost_reduction`/`_apply_cost_reduction` (only generic, clamped). `_resolve_spell` sets `card.chosen_targets = stack_obj.targets`, calls on_resolve, moves permanents to battlefield / non-permanents to graveyard. NOTE: NO firing of SpellCastTriggeredEvent here (must add).\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py` — `declare_attackers_step` taps attackers, sets is_attacking, but does NOT fire AttacksTriggeredEvent (must add). `_deal_damage` has `is_combat`/`combat` not tracked into trigger event clearly.\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` — `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller)`, `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker)`, `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` (NO player field), replacement events `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent(destination, controller, owner, prevented)` and subclasses.\n   - `/workspace/engine/game_state.py` — `extra_turns: list[int]` FIFO queue, `_normal_next_index`, `advance_phase()`. ENGINE LIMITATION noted: skip-turn interactions not fully handled. No begin-of-main-phase event.\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py` — `run_turn` fires `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()` at upkeep; no main phase event. `_do_draw_step` skips turn-1 starting player draw.\n   - `/workspace/engine/triggers.py` — `fire_event` collects matching triggers (empty = no-op, so adding fire_event calls is safe), APNAP ordering.\n   - `/workspace/engine/zones.py` — `move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, replacement_event=None)` central transition with trigger/replacement hooks. `move_zone` DELETES `colors_spent` on zone change.\n   - `/workspace/engine/game.py` — helpers: `deal_damage`, `destroy`, `sacrifice`, `exile`, `draw_card`, `discard`, `create_token(game, player, token)`, `add_counter`, `remove_counter`, `tap`, `untap`.\n   - `/workspace/test_utils.py` — `create_game(deck1, deck2, scripts=...)`, `set_board_state(game, player_index, battlefield=, hand=, graveyard=, life=, mana=)`, `cast_spell(game, player_index, card_name, targets=)`, `advance_to_phase`, `declare_attackers`, `declare_blockers`, `card_colors`.\n   - FDN reference patterns observed:\n     - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_205/card_impl.py` (Converge): `__init__` sets `self.colors_spent: int = 0`; `on_resolve` uses `count = self.colors_spent` then `range(count)`. Test sets `card.colors_spent = 2` as INT directly. IMPORTANT: must handle both int (test) and list (cast pipeline) — use `len(cs) if not isinstance(cs, int) else cs`.\n     - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_134/card_impl.py` & `fdn_44` (Planeswalker): `get_loyalty_abilities` returns `[LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost=+1, effect=_fn, description=...)]`; effects read `getattr(pw, '_resolve_target', None)`; legendary supertype + subtype added.\n     - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_57/card_impl.py` (cost_reduction): `def cost_reduction(self, game) -> int` counts board state, returns int (engine clamps to generic).\n     - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_48/card_impl.py` (Refute counterspell): `_counter_spell(game, stack_obj)` removes from `game.stack._items`, removes card from controller's STACK zone, adds to owner's graveyard. `can_cast`/`get_targets` iterate `game.stack.objects()`. `_get_chosen_target` reads `chosen_targets[0]` or `_resolve_target`.\n     - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_11/card_impl.py` & `fdn_37` (register_triggers): register `TriggerRegistration(event_type=..., condition=lambda game,event:..., effect=lambda game:..., source=self, controller=controller)`; per-turn tracking via attributes like `source._exemplar_drew_on_turn`.\n     - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_54/card_impl.py` (activated ability): `get_activated_abilities(self, game)` returns `[ActivatedAbility(cost=lambda game,src:..., effect=_fn, description=...)]`, sets `ability.tap_cost = True`.\n     - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_215/card_impl.py` (modal): `get_modes()` returns list of `Mode(name, description)`; reads `self.chosen_mode`; helper `_get_target`/`_get_targets`.\n     - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_53/card_impl.py` (Surveil): on_resolve manually implements surveil — look at top of library (`lib_cards[-1]`), `controller.choose_yes_no(...)`, move to graveyard if yes.\n     - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_13/card_impl.py` (Fleeting Flight): uses ContinuousEffect with `Layer.ABILITY`, `DURATION_END_OF_TURN` to grant flying; `_is_on_battlefield` helper.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Initial `python` command not found → used `python3` instead. Baseline test run: `python3 -m pytest -q` → 1184 passed, 25 warnings.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Confirmed `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` and `AttacksTriggeredEvent` exist but are never fired by the engine — will need to add `fire_event` calls in `cast_spell`/`cast_spell_free` (after pushing StackObject) and `declare_attackers_step` respectively. Verified this is safe because `fire_event` is a no-op when no matching triggers are registered, and engine_tests only test TriggerManager in isolation (test_triggers.py manually fires events).\n   - Identified Converge dual-type handling (int vs list for colors_spent).\n   - Identified Mana Sculpt needs total mana spent tracking (not currently tracked — only colors_spent list exists).\n   - Identified no \"beginning of main phase\" event for Mana Sculpt delayed mana / Improvisation Capstone Paradigm — will need engine extension.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - System reminders listing deferred tools (ToolSearch) and available skills.\n   - Main task message: \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json`... Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt`... You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics... Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - Tool-load confirmation message (\"Tool loaded.\").\n   - Final message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any