{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's explicit task (verbatim from prompt.md): \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly — they have rich docstrings: `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`. You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\"\n\n   CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS (must be preserved verbatim):\n   - \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - From AGENTS.md Hard Rules: \"Card location invariant — Each card's canonical implementation class must remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`. Do not move or rename card directories.\"\n   - \"Staged-test integrity — Treat `engine_tests/` as read-only... do not modify or delete any existing FDN reference test file at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py` (you may read them as examples, but never edit them)... Your own SOS tests belong at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\"\n   - \"Additive-only engine modifications — You may add new methods, classes, helpers, and files inside `engine/`. You may modify the bodies of existing functions to implement card behavior. You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/` — no renaming, no refactoring.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG card framework: `CardImpl` base with subclasses Creature, Instant, Sorcery, Enchantment, Aura, Artifact, ArtifactCreature, Planeswalker, Land.\n   - Hook methods: `can_cast(game)`, `cost_reduction(game)->int` (only reduces generic, clamped >=0), `on_cast(game)`, `on_resolve(game)`, `get_targets(game)->[TargetRequirement]`, `register_triggers(game)`, `register_replacement_effects(game)`, `get_activated_abilities(game)`, `get_modes()`, `get_loyalty_abilities()` (Planeswalker), `get_mana_abilities()` (Land).\n   - Triggered abilities: `TriggerManager.register(TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller))`, `fire_event(game, event)` (no-op if no matching triggers), APNAP ordering. Events are dataclasses in events.py.\n   - Replacement effects: `ReplacementManager.register(ReplacementEffect(event_type, source, condition, replacement, controller))`, `apply(game, event)`; \"instead\" semantics; move_to_zone consults them on battlefield-exit with destination redirect/prevented.\n   - Continuous effects (TWO classes): `engine.card.ContinuousEffect(apply, remove, description)` [legacy] vs `engine.continuous_effects.ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration)` [layer system, used by FDN/EffectManager]. Layers IntEnum (COPY=1..POWER_TOUGHNESS=7), SubLayer (7a-7d), DURATION_PERMANENT=-1, DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0. `EffectManager.add/apply_all/remove_expired`.\n   - colors_spent: set by cast_spell to `list(mana_pool.last_payment_colors)`; move_zone DELETES it on zone change. Converge cards handle both int (test) and list (pipeline).\n   - mana_spent: NEW — now set by cast_spell to `mana_pool.last_payment_total`.\n   - DeterministicPlayer: FIFO `_script` deque for choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card/assign_damage_order; test helpers prepend via `player._script.appendleft(...)`.\n   - Loyalty abilities: card returns list[LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)]; effect takes (game); reads `getattr(pw,'_resolve_target',None)`. abilities.py has activate_ability/LoyaltyAbilityInstance with sorcery-speed + once-per-turn restriction (`_loyalty_activated_this_turn`).\n   - Mechanics needing engine work: Converge, Surveil, Miracle, Casualty, Affinity, Paradigm, Prepared, coin flips, skip turns. None of these (except evergreens) are in the Keyword enum.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` — ADDED `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=None, precombat=False)` after `BeginningOfCombatTriggeredEvent`. Needed for Mana Sculpt delayed mana and Improvisation Capstone Paradigm. (DONE)\n   - `/workspace/engine/mana.py` — ADDED `self._last_payment_total: int = 0` to __init__; ADDED `last_payment_total` property; in `pay()` compute total: \n     ```python\n     colors_spent: set[Color] = set()\n     total_spent = 0\n     for mt, old_amount in self._pool.items():\n         new_amount = working.get(mt, 0)\n         if new_amount < old_amount:\n             total_spent += old_amount - new_amount\n             if mt in _MANA_TO_COLOR:\n                 colors_spent.add(_MANA_TO_COLOR[mt])\n     self._last_payment_colors = sorted(colors_spent, key=lambda c: c.value)\n     self._last_payment_total = total_spent\n     self._pool = working\n     return True\n     ```\n     (DONE) Needed for Mana Sculpt (\"mana spent to cast that spell\").\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — In `cast_spell`, after setting `card.colors_spent`, ADDED `card.mana_spent = player.mana_pool.last_payment_total` and after `game.stack.push(stack_obj)` ADDED:\n     ```python\n     from engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n     game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n         game,\n         SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player),\n     )\n     ```\n     (DONE) Needed for Silverquill casualty, Great Hall pump, prowess-style triggers. Verified no-op when no triggers registered.\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py` — `declare_attackers_step` taps attackers, sets is_attacking, registers in combat.attackers — but does NOT fire AttacksTriggeredEvent (STILL NEEDS EDIT for The Dawning Archaic). `_deal_damage` records damage_assignments.\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py` — `run_turn` loop fires BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent at upkeep. Main phases (PRECOMBAT_MAIN/POSTCOMBAT_MAIN, step None) fire NO event (STILL NEEDS EDIT to fire BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent). `_do_draw_step` skips turn-1 starting player draw.\n   - `/workspace/engine/zones.py` — `move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, *, replacement_event=None)`. Fires Leaves/CreatureDies on battlefield exit (before unregister), registers triggers/replacement effects + fires EntersBattlefield on entry. `_DESTINATION_ZONE_MAP` maps \"graveyard/exile/hand/library\". `move_zone` deletes colors_spent.\n   - `/workspace/engine/stack.py` — `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets=None)` shallow-copies source card, binds on_resolve to call copied_card.on_resolve directly (no zone move) — use for Silverquill casualty copy. `StackObject(source, controller, targets, on_resolve, is_mana_ability)`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/game.py` — helpers: deal_damage, destroy, sacrifice, exile, draw_card, discard, create_token(game, player, token), add_counter(game, perm, \"+1/+1\"|\"-1/-1\"|\"loyalty\", amount), remove_counter, tap, untap. create_token sets is_token/owner/controller, adds to battlefield, fires ETB, registers triggers.\n   - `/workspace/engine/abilities.py` — activate_ability dispatches LoyaltyAbilityInstance (sorcery speed, once/turn via _loyalty_activated_this_turn) vs ActivatedAbilityInstance. tap_cost(game, source) helper.\n   - FDN reference patterns (read this session