{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VxYicjhxuofuUPNSoYM8f2","type":"tool_result","content":"160\t    8. **Push StackObject** — push a :class:`StackObject` whose\n161\t       ``on_resolve`` callback handles resolution.\n162\t\n163\t    Raises:\n164\t        CastingError: If any legality check fails.\n165\t    \"\"\"\n166\t    # 1. Timing\n167\t    if not can_cast_at_instant_speed(card) and not is_sorcery_speed(game, player):\n168\t        raise CastingError(\n169\t            f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — sorcery-speed timing not met\"\n170\t        )\n171\t\n172\t    # 2. can_cast\n173\t    if not card.can_cast(game):\n174\t        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — can_cast returned False\")\n175\t\n176\t    # 3. Hand check\n177\t    hand = game.get_hand(player)\n178\t    if not hand.contains(card):\n179\t        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — card not in hand\")\n180\t\n181\t    # 4. Move card from hand to stack zone\n182\t    stack_zone = player.zones[Zone.STACK]\n183\t    hand.remove(card)\n184\t    stack_zone.add(card)\n185\t\n186\t    # Clear any stale colors_spent from a prior cast before new payment.\n187\t    if hasattr(card, \"colors_spent\"):\n188\t        del card.colors_spent\n189\t\n190\t    # 5. Choose targets\n191\t    target_specs = card.get_targets(game)\n192\t    chosen_targets: list[Any] = []\n193\t    if target_specs:\n194\t        for spec in target_specs:\n195\t            target = player.choose_target(target_specs, spec)\n196\t            # Validate against filter_fn if the spec provides one\n197\t            filter_fn = getattr(spec, \"filter_fn\", None)\n198\t            if filter_fn is not None and target is not None:\n199\t                if not filter_fn(target):\n200\t                    stack_zone.remove(card)\n201\t                    hand.add(card)\n202\t                    raise CastingError(\n203\t                        f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — chosen target does not \"\n204\t                        f\"satisfy filter: {getattr(spec, 'description', '')}\"\n205\t                    )\n206\t            chosen_targets.append(target)\n207\t\n208\t    # 5b. Protection check — reject targets that have protection from this\n209\t    #     spell (the T in DEBT).\n210\t    from engine.protection import has_protection_from\n211\t\n212\t    for target in chosen_targets:\n213\t        if has_protection_from(target, card):\n214\t            # Rollback: move card from stack zone back to hand\n215\t            stack_zone.remove(card)\n216\t            hand.add(card)\n217\t            raise CastingError(\n218\t                f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — target has protection from this spell\"\n219\t            )\n220\t\n221\t    # Targets are stored on the StackObject (not the card) and passed\n222\t    # through the resolve pipeline via on_resolve(game, targets=...).\n223\t\n224\t    # 6. Mana check / payment (rollback on failure)\n225\t    # Ensure the card knows its controller so that cost_reduction() hooks\n226\t    # (e.g. Embercleave counting attacking creatures you control) see the\n227\t    # casting player, even for cards that were added to hand without an\n228\t    # explicit controller assignment.\n229\t    if card.controller is None:\n230\t        card.controller = player\n231\t    reduction = get_cost_reduction(game, card, player)\n232\t    effective_cost = _apply_cost_reduction(card.mana_cost, reduction) if reduction > 0 else card.mana_cost\n233\t\n234\t    if not player.mana_pool.can_pay(effective_cost):\n235\t        # Rollback: move card from stack zone back to hand\n236\t        stack_zone.remove(card)\n237\t        hand.add(card)\n238\t        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — insufficient mana\")\n239\t\n240\t    # TODO: Phase 3 — support player choice for generic mana payment to optimize Converge color count\n241\t    player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost)\n242\t\n243\t    # Store colors of m