{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Verbatim from prompt.md (from prior session): \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly — they have rich docstrings: `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`. You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\"\n\n   CRITICAL CONSTRAINTS (preserve verbatim):\n   - \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n   - From AGENTS.md Hard Rules: \"Card location invariant — Each card's canonical implementation class must remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`. Do not move or rename card directories.\"\n   - \"Staged-test integrity — Treat `engine_tests/` as read-only... do not modify or delete any existing FDN reference test file at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`... Your own SOS tests belong at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\"\n   - \"Additive-only engine modifications — You may add new methods, classes, helpers, and files inside `engine/`. You may modify the bodies of existing functions to implement card behavior. You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/` — no renaming, no refactoring.\"\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG framework: CardImpl base + subclasses Creature, Instant, Sorcery, Land, Planeswalker, Artifact, etc.\n   - Hooks: `can_cast(game)`, `cost_reduction(game)->int` (reduces generic only, clamped >=0), `grant_cost_reduction(game,card,controller)->int` (additive engine hook), `on_cast(game)`, `on_resolve(game)`, `get_targets(game)->[TargetRequirement]`, `register_triggers(game)`, `get_activated_abilities(self)->[ActivatedAbility]` (NO game arg in base), `get_mana_abilities(self)->[ManaAbility]`, `get_loyalty_abilities(self)->[LoyaltyAbility]`.\n   - ETB convention: permanent ETB effects implemented via `on_resolve` + `get_targets` (on_resolve runs while card still on stack, before move to battlefield; the card's own register_triggers fires AFTER the ETB event so a self ETB trigger won't catch its own entry).\n   - ManaAbility(cost: (game,src)->bool, mana_produced: (game)->None, description); ActivatedAbility(cost: (game,src)->bool, effect: (game)->None, description); LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect: (game)->None, description).\n   - Triggers: TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition: (game,event)->bool, effect: (game)->None, source, controller); effect does NOT receive event (stash state on source in condition). fire_event pushes matching trigger effects onto the STACK (APNAP order); condition runs immediately; resolve_top/stack resolution runs effects.\n   - Events: SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller), AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker), DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card), BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent() [NO fields — use game.active_player], BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, precombat), EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent(permanent, controller), CreatureDiesTriggeredEvent, EndOfTurnTriggeredEvent/EndStepTriggeredEvent (NOT fired by turn.py).\n   - Continuous effects: ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply: (game)->None, timestamp, duration). EffectManager.add/remove_expired/apply_all. apply_all calls `_reset_characteristics()` on all battlefield objects (resets card_types to `_original_card_types`, keywords), then applies sorted effects. Layer: COPY=1..POWER_TOUGHNESS=7. SubLayer 7a CHARACTERISTIC_DEFINING/7b SET_PT/7c MODIFY_PT/7d COUNTERS. DURATION_PERMANENT=-1, DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0. Cleanup step calls remove_expired+apply_all.\n   - copy_spell(game, original: StackObject, controller, new_targets=None) shallow-copies source card. cast_spell(game,player,card) pays full cost. cast_spell_free(game,player,card,from_zone) casts free. resolve_top(game) pops+resolves stack top.\n   - Game helpers (engine.game): deal_damage, destroy, sacrifice, exile(game,obj), draw_card, discard(game,player,card), create_token(game,player,token), add_counter, tap, untap.\n   - move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, *, replacement_event=None); entering battlefield uses controller as dest_player, registers triggers, fires ETB.\n   - `_replace_graveyard_with_exile` flag honored in casting.py `_resolve_spell` (exiles instead of graveyard after on_resolve, consumed once).\n   - ManaPool: no restricted-mana support; last_payment_colors, last_payment_total. cast_spell sets card.colors_spent (list) and card.mana_spent; move clears colors_spent.\n   - cards_drawn_this_turn tracked but NEVER reset.\n   - DeterministicPlayer._script deque; choose/choose_yes_no/choose_card/choose_target/assign_damage_order all pop front; `p._script.extend([...])`. test_utils.create_game(deck1,deck2,scripts=(s1,s2)), set_board_state(game,idx,battlefield/hand/graveyard/life/mana).\n   - Keyword flags include FLYING, HASTE, VIGILANCE, DEATHTOUCH, REACH, etc. Supertype.LEGENDARY.\n   - Registry imports card class by EXACT class name from card_impl — must preserve template class names.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/engine/game_state.py` — EDITED (additive skip-turn). Added in __init__ after `self._normal_next_index: int = 1`:\n     ```python\n     # Skip-turn counters keyed by player seat index. ...\n     self.skip_turns: dict[int, int] = {}\n     ```\n     And in advance_phase end-of-turn branch replaced the else with:\n     ```python\n     else:\n         candidate = self._normal_next_index\n         if self.skip_turns.get(candidate, 0) > 0:\n             self.skip_turns[candidate] -= 1\n             if self.skip_turns[candidate] <= 0:\n                 del self.skip_turns[candidate]\n             self.active_player_index = 1 - candidate\n         else:\n             self.active_player_index = candidate\n             self._normal_next_index = 1 - candidate\n     ```\n     Default empty dict → identical to prior behavior. Verified 1184 pass.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py` — WROTE GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land). Two ManaAbilities ({T}:{C} via `_tap_only`+`_add_colorless`; {T}+pay 1 life: any color via `_tap_and_pay_life`+`_add_any_color` using controller.choose over `_COLOR_MANA` tuple). get_activated_abilities returns {5} ability (`_cost` pays {5}, `_effect` calls `source._animate(game)` if not already creature). `_animate` sets base_power=2/base_toughness=4, calls `_apply_animation`, adds permanent ContinuousEffect at Layer.TYPE (re-adds CREATURE+Wizard, sets modified P/T), registers pump trigger. `_register_pump_trigger`: SpellCastTriggeredEvent for instant/sorcery by controller → `source.modified_power += 1` + EOT ContinuousEffect at Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS/SubLayer.MODIFY_PT. Defines power/toughness @property and `_reset_characteristics` (super + reset modified to base). Has base/modified_power/toughness, plus/minus counters, damage_marked, is_attacking/blocking, summoning_sick, is_token in __init__.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` — WROTE LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature) {3}{R}{W} 5/5 FLYING|HASTE Legendary {Elder,Dragon}. register_triggers: miracle (DrawsCardTriggeredEvent; condition checks on-battlefield, player is controller, first-draw-this-turn via `ctrl._lorehold_miracle_turn` vs game.turn_number, drawn card instant/sorcery, stashes `source._miracle_card`; effect: can_pay {2}, choose_yes_no, pay {2}, cast_spell_free from HAND) + loot (BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent; condition on-battlefield + game.active_player is not ctrl; effect: choose_yes_no, choose_card discard, draw_card). Helper `_on_battlefield`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py` — WROTE RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker) {1}{B}{B} starting_loyalty=3 Legendary {Ral}. `_flip_heads(game,count)` uses `game.coin_flip_results` override list else `random.random()<0.5`. get_loyalty_abilities: +1 surveil 2 (loop top card choose_yes_no→graveyard), -1 each player discard (choose_yes_no per player, player.choose_card), -2 reanimate (creature MV<=3 from controller graveyard, set controller/summoning_sick=True, move_to_zone GY→BATTLEFIELD), -7 (`_flip_heads(game,5)`, `game.skip_turns[idx] += heads`).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py` — WROTE ImprovisationCapstone(Sorcery) {5}{R}{R} subtype Lesson. on_resolve: `_do_capstone` then if not `_is_paradigm_copy`: `_register_paradigm` + set `_replace_graveyard_with_exile=True`. `_do_capstone`: exile library top until total MV>=4, choose_yes_no/choose_card loop to cast_spell_free from EXILE. `_register_paradigm`: BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent (precombat, controller, source in exile) → choose_yes_no, copy.copy(source) with `_is_paradigm_copy=True`, push StackObject. Helpers `_mana_value`, `_is_castable_spell` (not LAND).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py` — WROTE EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature) {1}{W}{W} 3/3 {Cat,Cleric}, `_prepared=False`. get_targets: target player (`_is_player`). on_resolve: create_token Inkling (1/1 FLYING via `_make_inkling`, colors {\"W\",\"B\"}) under target player; `your_creatures = _count_creatures(controll